      "side": 1,
      "message": "Well, I was thinking that we could get here from binder_send_failed_reply() (transaction sender context) while at the same time the target_proc is entering binder_release() and triggering the deferred cleanup of the proc. The scenario would be:\n\n1) procA: binder_release() schedules deferred proc release\n2) procB: binder_send_failed_reply() --\u003e binder_free_transaction() with procA as target\n3) procA: binder_deferred_release() is called\n4) procB: acquire t-\u003elock (line 2123)\n5) procA: block on t-\u003elock while cleanup up active transactions\n6) procB: release t-\u003elock (line 2127)\n7) procA: acquire t-\u003elock, finish cleanup and free proc\n8) procB: acquire inner lock (line 2129). UAF.\n\nThe tmp_ref is to prevent freeing the proc at step #7 and deferring until we are done with the proc here. Do you think this is impossible?\n\nIn this scenario, the threads have all been freed and proc-\u003eis_dead \u003d\u003d true, so the proc would be cleaned up at the decrement (line 2133). I still don\u0027t think there is any other entity that would be taking out a tmp_ref on the proc...can you think of a case?",
